# REST API Rules (ADR-011)

## Every Custom Endpoint

- Register on `rest_api_init` with a versioned namespace:
  `bingocommerce/v1`.
- EVERY route has an explicit `permission_callback` performing a real check —
  `__return_true` on a mutating or data-exposing endpoint is rejected.
- EVERY parameter has `sanitize_callback` (and `validate_callback` where
  applicable).
- Any direct DB query inside an endpoint uses `$wpdb->prepare()`.
- Errors return safe messages — never expose SQL, stack traces, payment
  details, or secret material.

## Machine Authentication

- WooCommerce-specific integrations (POS sync): WooCommerce REST API Consumer
  Keys, scoped per integration with explicit Read / Write / Read-Write.
- Non-WooCommerce REST integrations: WordPress core Application Passwords
  (revocable per application).
- NEVER build custom API-key auth systems for machine clients (ADR-011 /
  anti-pattern list).

## Android Device API (QR redemption)

- No permanent hall-wide API key. Every device has: unique ID, hall (blog_id)
  assignment, its own revocable credential, status, last-seen timestamp
  (network-wide registry table, ADR-018).
- Device tokens are short-lived; a compromised device must be revocable
  without affecting other devices in that hall.
- Redemption endpoint must be: rate-limited, hall-scoped, and ATOMIC —
  validate hall, order, payment, session, expiry, refund/cancellation status,
  and device eligibility, then transition the ticket `issued` → `redeemed`
  and bind the device in one atomic operation. Repeated or simultaneous scans
  are rejected and logged.
- A second device can never redeem the same order unless a staff-gated
  reactivation cleared the binding first (BR-009, BR-010).

## Platform Hardening

- Unauthenticated `/wp/v2/users` is disabled network-wide (prevents hall staff
  username enumeration).
